    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0643" n="385" xml:id="pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/3230</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.30 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 7th.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d563-f1"/> No official answer yet to
                    suggestion that <hi rendition="#italic">Ogeechee</hi> cargo as whole to be dealt
                    with outside paragraph 5, order March 11. Meantime, convincing evidence of
                    American ownership, and especially that ownership passed prior to March 11, if
                    sent to me, may enable me as in two cases already settled, to effect immediate
                    release.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
